  "name": "Crucible Block",
  "description": "Weld it on a Foundry Core's +x side, or beside another Crucible Block: the Core splits its blocks into squares, each one crucible that tips to pour, and every square works at once. Each block of an n x n square adds 1 + n/4 to the Core's rate (a lone block 1.25, a 3 x 3's 1.75 each), so bigger squares pay more. A wrecked block keeps its square and adds nothing until mended. No power of its own: the Core draws a share for it.",
